::sanctions::country ns
meta {
    doc: """
    Country normalization for screening. The lists spell countries
    differently ("Burma", "Congo, Democratic Republic of the", "IR",
    "USSR (now Russian Federation)"), so every country is reduced to an
    ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code where one is known (Kosovo is `XK`), and to
    its normalized name otherwise.

    The name table comes from the public-domain tz `iso3166.tab`, the EU
    list's own code/description pairs, and the spellings used by the
    OFAC, UK and UN lists.
    """
}

::re ::hot::regex

